    "p:Online PDF tools are popular for good reason: merging, splitting and compressing a PDF takes a minute, and many let you start without an account. If you are here, you are probably after the same convenience with one thing changed. Either the document is private, or you keep hitting a limit on file size or on how many tasks you can run in a day.",
    "h:The one real difference: where your file goes",
    "p:Most online PDF services work by sending your file to their servers, processing it there, and letting you download the result. They typically say they delete files after a short time, and the details differ from one service to the next, so read the policy of whichever one you use. For a menu or a recipe that is fine. For a tenancy agreement, a bank statement, a medical report or an ID document, it means a copy of the file sits on someone else&rsquo;s computer for a while.",
